  "question": {
    "text": "If a flagstaff of 6 metres high placed on the top of a tower throws a shadow of \\(2 \\sqrt{3}\\) metres along the ground, then the angle (in degrees) that the sun makes with the ground is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "XSZrZ",
      "text": "\\(60^{\\circ}\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "7JH2p",
      "text": "\\(80^{\\circ}\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "yalCb",
      "text": "\\(75^{\\circ}\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "tOMCJ",
      "text": "None of these",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Accordingly,\n\\(\\tan \\theta=\\frac{h}{x}=\\frac{h+6}{x+2 \\sqrt{3}}=\\frac{6}{2 \\sqrt{3}} \\Rightarrow \\theta=60^{\\circ}\\)\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/tQkcpar07B9fqdYJWQ12ih7PgndRF2IP_v_OdhX8gvc.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\n[Since the triangles \\(A E C\\) and \\(B D C\\) are similar] \\(h \\cot \\alpha=(h-100) \\cot \\beta\\)\n\\(\\therefore h=\\frac{100 \\cot \\beta}{\\cot \\beta-\\cot \\alpha}\\)",
    "image": null
  },
